{
  "_readme": [
    "Numeric cases for app.compute_tab_totals and the percent discount of app.apply_discount.",
    "packages/db/tests/money-totals.test.ts proves the SQL against every case; tabTotals.test.ts runs every case through the TypeScript mirror.",
    "Rules (all integer IQD, prices include tax):",
    "  rd(n, d) = floor((2n + d) / (2d))   -- half-up division, n >= 0, d > 0",
    "  live lines = lines with voided = false, sorted by id ascending",
    "  subtotal S = sum(line_total of live lines)",
    "  discounts = discount_amount rows at their stored amount (fixed when applied);",
    "  percent_discounts = discount_percent rows, re-derived from the CURRENT S: rd(S * bps, 10000) each,",
    "                      so a void lowers them (their stored_amount is history only and never counts)",
    "  discount D = min(sum(discounts) + sum over percent rows of rd(S * bps, 10000), S); D = 0 when S = 0",
    "  per live line i, cum_i = running sum of line_total: alloc_i = rd(D * cum_i, S) - rd(D * cum_(i-1), S) (0 when S = 0)",
    "  per tax_rate_bps group r: net_r = sum(line_total - alloc); tax = sum over r of rd(net_r * r, 10000 + r)",
    "  total = S - D; paid = sum(payments); refunded = sum(refunds); due = max(total - paid, 0)",
    "  refunds never change due (a refund is money given back on a settled tab).",
    "  percent discount amount = min(rd(S * bps, 10000), S - existing_discount): what apply_discount answers and stores"
  ],
  "cases": [
